            <ArticleTitle>8-Methoxyquinoline-5-carboxamides as PDE4 inhibitors: a potential treatment for asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1613-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of bicyclic heteroaryl ring systems was considered as a replacement for the 3-cyclopentyloxy-4-methoxyphenyl moiety in rolipram resulting in the discovery of 8-methoxyquinoline-5-carboxamides as potent inhibitors of phosphodiesterase type 4 (PDE4).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
